# Design: --agent-script and the webclip participant

## Problem
Review-fix-plan item F5 requires a scripted participant to complete
the corrected webclip task through the public run command, read
returned identifiers, and send real Accept headers, with no guessed
fixture identifiers. The run command had no way to hand the mock
adapter a script.

## Approach
- loadAgentScript resolves the path against the command cwd, parses
  with parseJsonStrict, and runs validateMockScript plus
  validateScriptTemplates before preflight, so a broken participant
  fails at exit 2 before any batch directory is written.
- selectAdapter takes the script as a second argument; a script with
  a non-mock selector keeps the specific AgentScriptUnsupported code
  only for codex-cli, while a bogus selector stays AgentUnsupported.
- The happy script (mock-participant.json) sends nine requests, every
  one with credentialName OAL_AUTH_BEARER because the gateway verifies
  the declared security alternative per request even though the pack
  sets security.enforce false.
- The failing script requests a clip id that cannot exist, receives
  404, and fails with MOCK_HTTP_STATUS_MISMATCH, which the runner maps
  to agent_failed through OAL-AGENT-EXIT-NONZERO.

## Gotchas
- Determinism proof needs the same --batch id and --cohort-seed in two
  separate workspaces: deriveTrialSeed mixes in the run id, so two
  different batch ids legitimately diverge (render duration_ms).
- oal replay --verify cannot replay scenario runs yet: replayRun
  rebuilds a stateless fixture gateway and the frozen inputs lack the
  behavior module. Follow-up task, not fixed here.

